// Tests of front::parser (#1219, A6 of track A of #1112): the whole parser on the language corpus. Every `.smith` file
// of every case folder of tests/smith-lang/cases (the corpus is the specification) is read with `parser::parse`, and
// each has one outcome, written to the golden tests/front/parser/corpus.txt as one line `case/path: outcome`:
//
//   ok                  parsed with no error; its dump is not empty and a second parse gives the same dump
//   error: <message> (line:column)   the parser's first error; the file must be in `allowed` (a case that is meant to
//   fail to
//                       parse, or a construct the plan removed), else the test fails
//   C, out of scope     no `module` line, or a `#` line: C under the C rule, reported and not parsed
//   skipped: <reason>   only for a decision not yet made; the reason names the issue
//
// The golden ends with `total N, ok N, error N, C N, skipped N`. The golden is written by running the test with the
// environment variable FRONT_UPDATE=1 (`smith test --update` is not available for test-front yet). Cases that mix a
// `.smith` file with other files: only the `.smith` files are read.
module front_parser_test;

import front::ast;
import front::parser;
import std::arena;
import std::env;
import std::files;
import std::format;
import std::mem;
import std::slice;
import std::test;

// The files the parser rejects, in four classes, one path a line (#1219). A: a gap in the parsers of A3 to A5, reported
// to the track A orchestrator; B: a construct the plan removed that the corpus still spells (the corpus stays: today's
// lowering reads it); C: a construct the plan has not decided, reported to the lead; D: a case that is meant to fail.
// An error that is in no class, or a listed file that parses, fails the test; a change to the parsers shows here and in
// the golden.
